  "term": "dynamic equilibrium",
  "definition": "In this historical source, dynamic equilibrium means a proposed balance point defined by equal rates of ongoing activity rather than by fixed amounts. The example given is a “normal price” at which production and consumption proceed at the same rate, though the source notes that finding such a balance is complex and uncertain.",
